# Build output.
bin/
obj/

# Publish output and the deployment zip. Regenerated by scripts/deploy-app.sh; a ~5 MB zip has no
# business in git.
artifacts/

# Scratch space used by scripts/prove-no-secrets.sh. It is deleted by a trap on exit, so this only
# matters if the script is killed mid-run.
.proof-tmp/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Nothing in this directory needs to be ignored for SECRECY, which is the point of the day.
#
# There is no .env, no local.settings.json, no parameter file holding a credential, and no
# @secure() value anywhere. Everything committed here is a public identifier: a client id, an
# object id, a hostname, a queue name. The only genuine secret involved lives in Key Vault, was
# generated by the deploy script, and never passed through a file.
#
# The entries above are all about build noise and size.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
